DISCOVERY DEMAND E — DOCKET METADATA & JUDGMENT DELAY

CASE: 1FDV-23-0001009
TO: Scot Stuart Brower, Esq. (Mother's Counsel)

DEFENDANT DEMANDS complete production of:

1. Digital timestamps of ALL docket entries
2. All draft orders prepared by mother's counsel
3. All communications between Judge's staff and mother's counsel
4. Proof that judgment was entered via JEFS (electronic filing timestamp)
5. Proof that clerk actually recorded judgment within 30 days
6. Any Rule 58(a) certification showing entry date
7. All amendments or corrections to the judgment after entry

RESPONSE DUE: 14 calendar days from service
FORMAT: Native electronic file format + electronic metadata

STATUTORY BASIS: HRS Rule 58(a) requires judgment entry within 30 days. If mother cannot produce proof of entry, the judgment is void under HRS Rule 60(b)(4). If entry was delayed, grounds for Rule 60(b)(4) void judgment motion and appeal bond reduction.
